  "attempt": "For even N and fixed squarefree W, let U_(N,W) be the reflection-symmetric functions that are constant on the residue orbits generated by a mod W and N-a mod W, and let u be the orthogonal projection of the prime-only theta vector onto U_(N,W). Then <theta,R_N theta>=||u||^2+||P_+(theta-u)||^2-||P_-(theta-u)||^2, so ||u||^2>||theta-u||^2 is a sufficient Goldbach certificate. For every fixed W, the prime number theorem in arithmetic progressions gives ||u||^2=O_W(N), while ||theta||^2 is asymptotic to N log N. Therefore the projection energy fraction tends to zero and no fixed wheel can satisfy this L2 certificate for all large endpoints. The exact local support count is product over p|W of p-1 when p|N and p-2 otherwise.",
